    "narrative": "The highlight of today\u2019s card is undoubtedly **Lawrence Butler**, who commands our highest efficiency score at 74.54. His matchup against Jared Jones provides a rare confluence of a neutral SP skill profile and a +10% park factor advantage, bolstered further by a favorable platoon split and his prime leadoff role. While **Geraldo Perdomo** (62.70) and **Tyler Freeman** (61.33) also clear the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, **Lawrence Butler** remains the primary engine for our offensive production today. **Tyler Freeman** represents a particularly intriguing start; despite facing a formidable arm in Shota Imanaga, the +5% wind-out factor and his favorable spot at the top of the order outweigh the risks associated with the opposing hurler's efficiency.\n\nRegarding the remaining core, **Bryson Stott** (59.62) sits right on the precipice of \"Strong\" territory. His value is tethered to the matchup against Ryan Gusto, where his dynamic platoon advantage (+13%) and the high-SB environment created by the pitcher's delivery mechanics make him a critical asset for us, even if his #7 batting order position acts as a slight drag on his ceiling. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Jonathan Aranda** (55.90) and **Masyn Winn** (54.09). While **Masyn Winn** lacks a specific confirmed SP opponent today, his leadoff placement keeps his floor stable. **Jonathan Aranda** faces Eric Lauer, and although the expected ERA of 4.63 suggests a favorable environment, the platoon disadvantage against the lefty creates enough volatility that we are tempering expectations.\n\nThe bench decision process was hampered significantly by our current IL cluster, as **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, and **Will Smith** remain sidelined, severely limiting our flexibility. Among the active bench, **Brendan Donovan** and **Matt Chapman** were the closest to cracking the starting lineup, but they ultimately fell short due to unfavorable projected matchups that failed to clear the 55-point mark required to displace our current starters. We are proceeding with caution given the \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board; should the official batting orders deviate significantly from our projections\u2014particularly for **Gleyber Torres** or **Jonathan Aranda**\u2014we will re-evaluate the utility of our bench depth to maximize our daily game caps.",
